---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { atlas as idx } from "../lib/atlas.js";
import provs from "../../public/providers.json";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import full from "../data/places-full.json";
import "../styles/kit.css";
/* EVERY NUMBER ON THIS PAGE IS COUNTED, as on /start/. The one typed fact is the start month. The donation link lives in
   src/data/site.json (support.url): it is a hosted Stripe Payment Link, so the payment happens on Stripe's page and this page
   never sees a card. check-data.py refuses the sandbox link (/test_), so the page cannot ship with it. */
const dots = idx.places.length;
const countries = new Set(full.places.map((p) => p.country).filter(Boolean)).size;
const sources = provs.providers.length;
const url = site.support?.url || "";
---
<Base
  title="Support Record Atlas"
  eyebrow="Free to use, and free to keep"
  dek="What this project is, what it takes to keep it going, and what a gift does. Nothing on the atlas is locked, whether or not you give.">

  <div class="sp-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="sp-big">Record Atlas is free. No paywall, no account, no subscription, and that will not change.</p>
      <p class="sp-small">It is kept going by one person. If it has saved you an evening, a gift of any size helps.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="sp-cta"><a class="sp-btn" href={url} rel="noopener">Give a gift</a>
      <span>You choose the amount. Paid on Stripe's own page; this site never sees your card.</span></p>
  </div>

  <ul class="k-grid sp-stats" aria-label="The atlas in numbers">
    <li class="k-card"><b>{dots.toLocaleString()}</b><span>places</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>{countries}</b><span>countries</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>{sources.toLocaleString()}</b><span>sources</span></li>
    <li class="k-card"><b>Sept 2026</b><span>started</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="k-lede sp-lede">Each source is read, placed on the map, checked against the place's name in the year of the record, and marked with what it costs to look. Every figure is counted from the data, never typed, and a build that finds a gap stops rather than publishing it.</p>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>About this</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-grid sp-three">
    <li class="k-card"><h3>About me</h3><p>I am David Defranceski. I research family history, mostly my own: the Defranceschi name, which runs from Istria and Dalmatia through Friuli to the Americas, and a few families I have been asked to help with. I do it on my own, with no institution behind me.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Why I built it</h3><p>Every family I worked on hit the same wall: which archive holds the register for a village, whether its images are free, and what the place was called in the year of the record. I built the atlas so that what one search learns is kept for the next.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Why it is free</h3><p>Research that only people who can pay can find is research that gets repeated. A paywall would have broken the one thing the atlas is for. I would rather it was used than earned from.</p></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>What it costs to run</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-grid sp-two">
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Hosting</h3><p>US$5 a month for Cloudflare's paid plan, which serves every page. It is billed per request once the site passes 10 million a month, so it grows as more people use it.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><h3>Records</h3><p>Some sources sit behind a subscription. When a question cannot be answered from free records I take one out for a month, rather than keep it running.</p></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>What a gift does</h2></div>
  <div class="k-hi is-plain">
    <p>A gift goes first to the hosting bill, then to the occasional month of a records subscription when a question needs one.</p>
    <p>A gift does not buy a feature, early access or a place in the queue. It keeps the atlas running and lets the work go on.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="sp-cta sp-end"><a class="sp-btn" href={url} rel="noopener">Give a gift</a>
  <span>You choose the amount. Stripe handles the payment.</span></p>

  <div class="k-foot">
    <p>Good to know</p>
    <p>A gift is a personal gift to the person who runs this atlas, not a tax-deductible donation to a charity.
    <a href={u("/privacy/")}>Privacy</a> · <a href={u("/start/")}>About the atlas</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .sp-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 18px 32px; align-items: center; padding: 26px 30px; border-radius: 24px; margin: 0 0 22px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--hue-wash), var(--panel)); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--hue) 28%, var(--rule)); }
  .sp-big { font: 800 clamp(22px, 3vw, 32px)/1.2 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -.02em; max-width: 26ch; margin: 0; }
  .sp-small { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 46ch; }
  .sp-cta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; margin: 0; }
  .sp-cta span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 26ch; line-height: 1.4; }
  .sp-btn { display: inline-block; background: var(--hue-solid); color: var(--on-hue); font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; padding: 14px 30px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 17px; box-shadow: 0 12px 24px -12px var(--hue-solid); }
  .sp-btn:hover, .sp-btn:focus-visible { filter: brightness(1.1); }
  .sp-end { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin: 22px 0 6px; }
  .sp-end span { max-width: none; }
  .sp-stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 140px), 1fr)); }
  .sp-stats .k-card { padding: 12px 14px; gap: 2px; border-radius: 16px; }
  .sp-stats b { font: 800 clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px)/1.1 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--hue-ink); }
  .sp-stats span { font: 600 11px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .sp-lede { margin: 14px 0 0; }
  .sp-three, .sp-two { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .sp-three { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr)); }
  .sp-two { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 320px), 1fr)); }
  .sp-three h3, .sp-two h3 { font-size: 20px; }
  main .k-hi { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; }
  main .k-foot { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .sp-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 20px; } }
</style>
